* This is when I was asked to reactivate Google Shopping as it was the only line of business generating revenue during the pandemic. 
* I had to:
   * Lead engineering through the transition to a new database (a decision I made) for the feed generation of Google Shopping. The old infrastructure was dismissed due to the layoffs, the old team was not in the company anymore and there was no handover.
   * When a new feed is added to Google Shopping every single item goes to review again and loses any history it had. This also can cause issues in particular with a new database. There were 11 issues across 15 countries. All fixed thanks to my lead by prioritising them based on impact, leading the engineer assigned (he didn’t have experience with MarTech). 
   * By Beginning of April the program was back running and Q2 2020 was the best quarter in the history of SEM Goods at Groupon. Even better than Q4. 
   * Also, I led the transition to a new 3rd party feed management tool with a 60% annual savings in fee for the company and the opportunity to be used by all paid channels globally at Groupon 




