Conversion API


One of the product marketing initiatives I’m most proud of is the one related to the Meta Conversion API (CAPI). The API allows advertisers to reduce the signal loss caused by enhanced privacy settings released over the years (one example: Apple iOS 14 update). When I started at Meta - second half of 2021 - the number of CAPI integrations in the EMEA Mid Market was declining. As CAPI lead in my region this is what I did:
* Look at data coming from Sales and identify the blockers for CAPI integration. Identifying 3 areas: Legal, Technical resources, Lack of urgency. Also, I created a list with top advertisers to focus on and led the taskforce and the tracking of the results.
* I worked on creating 3 different GTM per each blocker area. 
   * Legal. Creation of an externally sharable 2-pager written by Meta Legal answering the most common questions/doubt advertisers legal team had. Sales internal training on the 2-pager. 
   * Tech resources. Worked on sales internal training and external narratives for CAPI Gateway, a plug-in version of CAPI that didn’t require tech resources on advertiser side. Also coordinated Business Engineering open office hours where advertisers could be guided by engg in the integration via zoom call. 
   * Lack of urgency. Produced externally shareable narrative with performance proof points on benefits of adopting CAPI and what other products could be enabled when adopting the API. 
* The result was a +30% in CAPI integration HoH. 
